# OpenClaw Chat Command - Implementation Complete ✅
## Summary
Successfully implemented a new `chat` command for OpenClaw that provides a simple, terminal-based interface for interacting with the AI agent using existing providers and channels.
## What Was Built
### Core Implementation
- **File**: `openclaw-standalone/src/cli/chat-cli.ts` (~200 lines)
- **Integration**: Registered in command registry
- **Status**: ✅ Built, tested, and working
### Key Features
✅ Simple readline-based terminal interface
✅ Real-time streaming responses from AI
✅ Uses existing OpenClaw gateway infrastructure
✅ Supports all configured providers (Google Antigravity, etc.)
✅ Session management for conversation context
✅ Model override capability
✅ Optional channel delivery
✅ Graceful error handling and exit
## Quick Start
```bash
# 1. Start the gateway (if not already running)
bun scripts/run-node.mjs gateway
# 2. In another terminal, start chat
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat
# 3. Type your message and press Enter
# 4. Type 'exit' or 'quit' to leave
```
## Usage Examples
```bash
# Basic chat
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat
# Custom session (separate conversation context)
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --session work
# Different model
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --model google-antigravity/claude-opus-4-5-thinking
# Remote gateway
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --url ws://192.168.1.100:18789 --token YOUR_TOKEN
# Enable channel delivery (send responses to WhatsApp, Telegram, etc.)
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --deliver
```
