## Comparison: Chat vs TUI
t:7(Feature,Chat Command,TUI Command)[**Complexity**,Simple (~200 lines),Full-featured (~1000+ lines) **Interface**,Basic readline,Rich TUI with panels **Setup**,Zero config,May need setup **Use Case**,Quick chats,Extended sessions **Learning Curve**,Instant,Moderate **Dependencies**,Built-in,@mariozechner/pi-tui **Features**,Essential only,Full-featured]
## When to Use Chat vs TUI
### Use `chat` when:
- ✅ You want a quick conversation
- ✅ You're testing the agent
- ✅ You prefer simplicity
- ✅ You're debugging
- ✅ You want minimal setup
### Use `tui` when:
- ✅ You need full history view
- ✅ You want slash commands
- ✅ You need session management UI
- ✅ You prefer rich interface
- ✅ You're doing extended work
## Troubleshooting
### "Failed to connect to gateway"
```bash
# Start the gateway
bun scripts/run-node.mjs gateway
# Check if it's running
ps aux | grep gateway
netstat -an | grep 18789
```
### "Agent error"
```bash
# Check gateway logs
tail -f /tmp/openclaw/openclaw-*.log
# Verify configuration
cat ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json | grep -A 10 '"agents"'
# Run diagnostics
bun scripts/run-node.mjs doctor
```
### No response
```bash
# Check model configuration
cat ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json | grep model
# Verify provider credentials
bun scripts/run-node.mjs configure
```
